==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>, delay 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 93.33 seconds<sup>2,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Gilgamesh (Enemy)|Gilgamesh]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Dagshund]]s spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
**8 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
- [[Gilgamesh (Enemy)|Gilgamesh]] is a [[traitless]] enemy, meaning that most [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] [[Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] (and the Legend Rare, [[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Dusk]]/[[Izanami of Eventide|Eventide]]) will be very effective to keep him at bay, alongside with the [[Dagshund|Dagshunds]] and [[Celeboodle|Celeboodles]].

- [[Ramen Cat]] is an effective [[Meatshield class Cats|meatshield]] against the [[Gabriel|Gabriels]], and can still tank a few hits from the other enemies.

